        "text": "The rework is done. Everything green: 228 tests, three checks clean, 53 straw dogs listed with no diagnostics.\n\n**What changed since your message**\n- **No allowlist.** The file is deleted. Each of the nineteen unclaimed skills opens its body — after the frontmatter — with `<straw-dog until=\"…\" ticket=\"…\">Mechanism: not yet</straw-dog>`, the whole line inside the tag. `/recall` binds to 01-0020, `/edge` to 01-0010.0100, the rest to 01-0017.\n- **The reverse pass reads the skill**, not a file: 22 skills, 3 named, 19 claiming; a skill that is neither, or both, or named twice, is a diagnostic with the skill directory as its subject. The report's `allowlist` key is gone; `skills` carries `claims`.\n- **The rules that caused it, amended and reinstalled** — [rule failure 5](docs/rule-failures.md) opened and closed in the same pass:\n  - **R4** now names the shape: *a file listing what other files each say for themselves is an index, whatever it is called — an allowlist, a register, a manifest — and each entry belongs at its authored home, wrapped there if provisional.*\n  - **R6** no longer says *allowlist*: *a skill … says so on its first body line … no list holds it.* The noun in the rule was the cause — it said \"list\", so a list got built, and R4's \"index\" didn't fire on something declared as a record.\n- **Shelf, doc, evidence, RFC and both tickets** brought to the inline form; the `docs/` places are `.0140`'s check data again; the install spec's \"manifest reads the allowlist\" is flagged for `.0130` to correct.\n\n**Honest note on the leak check:** still `.0140`'s and unbuilt; the sweep says the eleven `not yet` links are gone from core's bare links (27 → 16), nothing finer.\n\n`commit=ask`. Commit as `IMPLEMENT: …`, then `/verify`?"
